+# `*-unknown-feos`
+
+**Tier: 3**
+
+Targets for [feos](https://github.com/kunaldawn/feos), a `no_std` Rust operating
+system for QEMU's AArch64 `virt` and x86_64 `q35` machines. User programs are static
+ELF executables over [relibc](https://gitlab.redox-os.org/redox-os/relibc), whose
+`platform/feos` maps POSIX onto feos's system calls.
+
+Target triples:
+
+- `x86_64-unknown-feos`
+- `aarch64-unknown-feos`
+
+## Target maintainers
+
+- Kunal Dawn ([@kunaldawn](https://github.com/kunaldawn))
+
+## Requirements
+
+These targets only support cross-compilation for now, and static executables only:
+`crt-static` is the default and the only linkage, programs are `ET_EXEC` linked at
+`0x1000400000` with every loadable segment on pages of its own, and `rust-lld` links
+them. x86_64 code is position independent (the image is beyond the small code model's
+reach) and uses no AVX or XSAVE state; AArch64 code is static and uses no outline
+atomics. `std` is supported (`panic=unwind` over LLVM's libunwind); threads,
+synchronisation, files, processes (`posix_spawn`) and time work, `std::net` needs
+the kernel's socket calls.
+
+The C side is relibc for feos, built as a sysroot with `crt0.o`, `crti.o`, `crtn.o`,
+`libc.a`, `libm.a` and `libcompiler_builtins.a`, and a C compiler driver for the
+target that finds them (`-print-file-name`).
+
+## Building the target
+
+Set the target's C compiler to a driver for the relibc sysroot and build `std` for it:
+
+```toml
+[build]
+target = ["x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu", "x86_64-unknown-feos", "aarch64-unknown-feos"]
+
+[rust]
+lld = true
+
+[target.x86_64-unknown-feos]
+cc = "/path/to/x86_64-unknown-feos-cc"
+cxx = "/path/to/x86_64-unknown-feos-cc"
+ar = "llvm-ar"
+ranlib = "llvm-ranlib"
+```
+
+Bootstrap builds LLVM's libunwind for the target and copies relibc's start files and
+libraries, found through the C compiler, into the target's library directory, where
+rustc looks for them.
+
+## Building Rust programs
+
+```sh
+cargo build --target x86_64-unknown-feos
+```
+
+The result runs on feos as it is (copy it into the image's `/bin`).
+
+## Testing
+
+The feos tree's `ports/test` boots both machines in QEMU and runs Rust programs and
+their checks in the feos shell. The Rust test suite is not run for these targets.
+
+## Cross-compilation toolchains and C code
+
+C code for these targets is built against the relibc sysroot with clang for
+`<arch>-unknown-none-elf`, `-D__feos__ -D__unix__`, `-fPIC` on x86_64.
